---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../../components/Nav.astro";
---

<Layout
  language="en"
  title="Integrated CRM & Customer Value | Karsten Uhlig"
  description="How I built integrated customer steering at bonprix and translated customer knowledge into operational decisions."
>
  <section class="crm-shell">
    <div class="crm-inner">
      <Nav language="en" homepage />
      <article class="crm-page">
        <header class="crm-hero">
          <p class="eyebrow">Commercial Management · CRM · Customer Value</p>
          <h1>Integrated CRM &amp; Customer Value</h1>
          <p class="hero-lead">Developing customer relationships economically.</p>
          <div class="hero-copy">
            <p>CRM means more to me than customer communications and campaigns. What matters is how a company develops its customer base: Which customers do we acquire? Whom do we want to retain or win back? Where is additional investment worthwhile – and where would it be unnecessary?</p>
            <p>Customer knowledge and economic decisions must therefore come together across Marketing, CRM, Commerce and other customer touchpoints.</p>
          </div>
          <p class="hero-principle">Not every channel should optimise for itself. What matters is what makes sense for the customer relationship and the business as a whole.</p>
        </header>

        <figure class="crm-overview" id="crm-overview">
          <a href="/images/integrated-customer-management-overview.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener" aria-label="Open the integrated customer management overview at full size">
            <img
              src="/images/integrated-customer-management-overview.png"
              alt="Integrated customer management: from customer knowledge through intelligence and operational activation to business impact, including the historical bonprix build and scale path."
              width="2172"
              height="724"
              loading="eager"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </a>
        </figure>

        <section class="page-section build-section" aria-labelledby="build-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-label">01 · Building the foundation</p>
            <h2 id="build-title">From data foundation to operational customer steering.</h2>
            <p>At bonprix, I played a major role in building integrated customer steering across several stages of development.</p>
          </div>

          <div class="fact-band" aria-label="Key facts about the platform build">
            <div><strong>2014</strong><span>first integrated marketing data platform</span></div>
            <div><strong>6 months</strong><span>to a shared operational foundation</span></div>
            <div><strong>around 10 teams</strong><span>involved in delivery</span></div>
          </div>

          <div class="build-copy">
            <p>The starting point was a fragmented data and marketing landscape. Customer records, transactions, email responses and web behaviour sat in separate systems, while channels often followed their own steering logic.</p>
            <p>As project lead, I led the cross-functional delivery and contributed directly to the data model, architecture decisions, target state and prioritisation of the first use cases.</p>
            <p>The platform connected campaign management, real-time personalisation and analytics. Shop, app and Paid Media followed, together with predictive approaches for purchase propensity, customer value, churn and recommendations.</p>
          </div>

          <ol class="build-path" aria-label="Historical development path">
            <li><span>Foundation</span><strong>Connect customer, transactional and behavioural data</strong></li>
            <li><span>Activation</span><strong>Operationalise segmentation and personalisation</strong></li>
            <li><span>Integration</span><strong>Link CRM, shop, app and Paid Media</strong></li>
            <li><span>Further development</span><strong>Make Predictive Decisioning usable internationally</strong></li>
          </ol>
        </section>

        <section class="page-section" aria-labelledby="practice-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-label">02 · Operational practice</p>
            <h2 id="practice-title">Three mechanisms that changed decisions.</h2>
          </div>

          <div class="practice-list">
            <article>
              <span>01</span>
              <div><h3>Behaviour-based email segmentation</h3><p>Current signals such as basket abandonment, product interest or recent interactions supplemented historical customer segments. This made it possible to respond more specifically to each customer situation.</p></div>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>02</span>
              <div><h3>Retargeting exclusions and avoiding unnecessary contacts</h3><p>CRM and response information became usable for Paid Media. Customers who had already engaged or purchased could be excluded deliberately instead of buying further paid contacts unnecessarily.</p></div>
            </article>
            <article>
              <span>03</span>
              <div><h3>Predictive Decisioning in CRM, newsletters, push and onsite</h3><p>Purchase propensity, customer value, churn and product recommendations were integrated into CRM, newsletters, push and onsite. A model only delivered value when its score changed a real decision at the right time.</p></div>
            </article>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="page-section challenge-section" aria-labelledby="challenge-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-label">03 · Real challenges</p>
            <h2 id="challenge-title">The difficult parts lay between data, operations and organisation.</h2>
          </div>
          <dl class="challenge-list">
            <div><dt>Identity</dt><dd>Different identifiers, cookie constraints and privacy requirements limited which customer signals could be connected reliably.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Operationalisation</dt><dd>Batch processing, real-time capability, interfaces and stable operations determined whether a score was available at the relevant moment.</dd></div>
            <div><dt>Adoption</dt><dd>Teams had to complement fixed campaign logic with hypotheses, experiments and model-assisted decisions. Clear accountability and visible results were central to this.</dd></div>
          </dl>
        </section>

        <section class="page-section contribution-section" aria-labelledby="contribution-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-label">04 · My contribution</p>
            <h2 id="contribution-title">Connecting economic logic, data and customer interaction.</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="contribution-copy">
            <p class="contribution-intro">I played a major role in building integrated customer steering at bonprix – from a shared customer understanding and the first marketing data platform to internationally scaled, data- and AI-enabled customer steering.</p>
            <p class="contribution-subhead">In doing so, I shaped the economic, domain and technological development:</p>
            <ul>
              <li><span class="contribution-number">01</span><div><strong>Built CRM capabilities</strong><span>and focused customer development more strongly on repeat purchase, customer value and economics.</span></div></li>
              <li><span class="contribution-number">02</span><div><strong>Co-designed the data foundation and architecture</strong><span>including the customer model, integration of touchpoints and prioritisation of the first use cases.</span></div></li>
              <li><span class="contribution-number">03</span><div><strong>Connected CRM, Marketing and Commerce</strong><span>so customer signals flowed directly into communication, personalisation and customer interactions.</span></div></li>
              <li><span class="contribution-number">04</span><div><strong>Established and scaled new capabilities</strong><span>from behaviour-based segmentation to Predictive Decisioning and international use.</span></div></li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        <section class="page-section closing-section" aria-labelledby="learning-title">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="section-label">05 · Implication</p>
            <h2 id="learning-title">Do not start with the platform.</h2>
            <p>First clarify how the customer base develops economically, which decisions are not good enough today and where a change will make the greatest difference. Then start with a small number of use cases, test the impact and scale successful solutions systematically.</p>
          </div>
          <blockquote>A shared data foundation is necessary. It only becomes decisive when people and systems use it to make better decisions together.</blockquote>
        </section>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  :global(body){background:#eef2f7}.crm-shell{width:100%;overflow:hidden;background:radial-gradient(circle at 86% 8rem,rgba(255,255,255,.78) 0,rgba(255,255,255,0) 30rem),linear-gradient(180deg,#eef2f7 0,#dce7f1 52rem,#eef2f7 108rem,#eef2f7 100%)}.crm-inner{max-width:1440px;margin:0 auto;padding:1.25rem 4.25rem 5rem}.crm-page{min-width:0;color:var(--color-ink)}.crm-page :where(h1,h2,h3,p,ul,blockquote,dl,dd){margin-top:0}.crm-hero{padding:1.4rem 0 3.5rem}.eyebrow,.section-label{color:var(--color-amber);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}.eyebrow{margin-bottom:1.2rem}.crm-hero h1{max-width:960px;margin-bottom:1.4rem;font-size:clamp(46px,5vw,66px);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.052em;line-height:.98}.hero-lead{max-width:780px;margin-bottom:1.8rem;font-size:clamp(23px,2.5vw,32px);letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.24}.hero-copy{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:clamp(2rem,5vw,6rem);max-width:1100px}.hero-copy p{margin-bottom:0;color:var(--color-body);font-size:16px;line-height:1.75}.hero-principle{max-width:980px;margin:2.5rem 0 0;padding:1.3rem 1.5rem;color:var(--color-ink);font-size:18px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.55;background:rgba(255,255,255,.48);border-left:3px solid var(--color-amber)}.crm-overview{margin:0 0 5.5rem}.crm-overview a{display:block;overflow:hidden;background:#fff;box-shadow:0 18px 50px rgba(15,45,78,.12);cursor:zoom-in}.crm-overview img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto}
  .page-section{padding:5.5rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)}.section-heading{max-width:920px;margin-bottom:3rem}.section-label{margin-bottom:.8rem}.section-heading h2{margin-bottom:.9rem;font-size:clamp(32px,3.7vw,48px);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.045em;line-height:1.06}.section-heading>p:last-child:not(.section-label){max-width:720px;margin-bottom:0;color:var(--color-body);font-size:16px;line-height:1.7}.fact-band{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);margin-bottom:3rem;border-block:1px solid var(--color-border)}.fact-band div{padding:1.5rem 1.6rem}.fact-band div+div{border-left:1px solid var(--color-border)}.fact-band strong,.fact-band span{display:block}.fact-band strong{color:var(--color-amber);font-size:26px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.03em}.fact-band span{max-width:240px;margin-top:.4rem;color:var(--color-body);font-size:12px;line-height:1.5}.build-copy{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr);gap:clamp(1.5rem,3vw,3rem)}.build-copy p{margin-bottom:0;color:var(--color-body);font-size:15px;line-height:1.75}.build-path{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:0;margin:3.5rem 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)}.build-path li{position:relative;padding:1.4rem 1.2rem 0 1.4rem}.build-path li::before{position:absolute;top:-4px;left:0;width:7px;height:7px;background:var(--color-amber);border-radius:50%;content:""}.build-path li+li{border-left:1px solid var(--color-border)}.build-path span,.build-path strong{display:block}.build-path span{color:var(--color-amber);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em;text-transform:uppercase}.build-path strong{margin-top:.5rem;font-size:14px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.5}
  .practice-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem)}.practice-list article{padding-top:1.4rem;border-top:2px solid rgba(30,60,100,.28)}.practice-list article>span{display:block;margin-bottom:1.5rem;color:var(--color-amber);font-size:11px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.12em}.practice-list h3{margin-bottom:.9rem;font-size:23px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.2}.practice-list p{margin-bottom:0;color:var(--color-body);font-size:15px;line-height:1.75}.challenge-list{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:clamp(2rem,4vw,4rem);margin-bottom:0}.challenge-list>div{padding-top:1.4rem;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border)}.challenge-list dt{margin-bottom:.9rem;color:var(--color-ink);font-size:22px;font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.025em}.challenge-list dd{margin-bottom:0;color:var(--color-body);font-size:15px;line-height:1.75}.contribution-copy{max-width:1120px}.contribution-copy .contribution-intro{max-width:900px;margin-bottom:0;color:var(--color-body);font-size:18px;line-height:1.72}.contribution-copy .contribution-subhead{max-width:900px;margin:1.6rem 0 0;color:var(--color-ink);font-size:16px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.65}.contribution-copy ul{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:2.3rem 0 0;padding:0;list-style:none}.contribution-copy li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:36px minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem;min-height:150px;padding:1.45rem;background:rgba(255,255,255,.44);border:1px solid var(--color-border-soft);border-top:2px solid rgba(30,60,100,.34)}.contribution-number{padding-top:.15rem;color:var(--color-amber);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:600;letter-spacing:.1em}.contribution-copy li strong,.contribution-copy li div>span{display:block}.contribution-copy li strong{color:var(--color-ink);font-size:17px;font-weight:600;line-height:1.4}.contribution-copy li div>span{margin-top:.55rem;color:var(--color-body);font-size:14px;line-height:1.65}.closing-section blockquote{max-width:1000px;margin:0;padding:1.6rem 0 0 1.6rem;font-size:clamp(22px,2.4vw,31px);font-weight:500;letter-spacing:-.025em;line-height:1.38;border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);border-left:3px solid var(--color-amber)}
  @media(max-width:900px){.build-copy{grid-template-columns:1fr}.build-path{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);row-gap:1.5rem}.build-path li:nth-child(3){border-left:0}.practice-list,.challenge-list{grid-template-columns:1fr}.practice-list article,.challenge-list>div{max-width:760px}}
  @media(max-width:768px){.crm-inner{padding:2rem 1.5rem 3rem}.crm-hero{padding:1rem 0 2.5rem}.hero-copy{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:1rem}.hero-principle{font-size:16px}.crm-overview{width:calc(100% + 3rem);margin:0 -1.5rem 4rem}.crm-overview a{overflow-x:auto;box-shadow:0 12px 32px rgba(15,45,78,.12);scrollbar-width:thin}.crm-overview img{width:1100px;max-width:none}.page-section{padding:4rem 0}.section-heading{margin-bottom:2rem}.fact-band{grid-template-columns:1fr}.fact-band div+div{border-top:1px solid var(--color-border);border-left:0}.build-path{grid-template-columns:1fr}.build-path li+li,.build-path li:nth-child(3){border-left:0}.practice-list,.challenge-list{gap:2.6rem}.practice-list article>span{margin-bottom:1rem}.contribution-copy .contribution-intro{font-size:16px}.contribution-copy ul{grid-template-columns:1fr}.contribution-copy li{min-height:0;padding:1.25rem}.closing-section blockquote{padding-left:1.2rem}}
</style>
